---
# yamllint disable rule:line-length
# The reference half of 123: a captured REFERENCE is already an Object, so nothing
# has to happen before `List.add` takes it. The Φ.hone.cap-box marker 114/118 left
# in state-acc is simply dropped, leaving the append as `dup; aload k; List.add;
# pop` — the same shape the dedicated reference peel produced before the marker
# split, and one slot shorter than a primitive's boxed append.
#
# The type code is a whole "L…;" descriptor here, which is what tells this rule
# apart from 123's "I"/"J"/"D". Neither rule depends on the other's fixpoint: each
# clears its own markers wherever they stand.
name: cap-box-reference
pattern: |
  ⟦
    𝐵-before,
    𝜏-box ↦ ⟦ φ ↦ Φ.hone.cap-box, code ↦ 𝑒-code ⟧,
    𝐵-after
  ⟧
result: |
  ⟦
    𝐵-before,
    𝐵-after
  ⟧
when:
  matches: ['^L[^;]*;$', 𝑒-code]
